{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1515710-minicomp-moniker","id":1515710,"title":"Minicomp Moniker","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-20T19:04:21-07:00","id":1515710,"title":"Minicomp Moniker","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Century Gothic\">Something that I have always wanted to alter about Trinity is the minicomp.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Century Gothic\">Trinity was written in the late 90s. Even though the term smartphone really didn\u2019t exist until the early 2000s, I do think that the idea for minicomps was predictive on the part of the authors, and I liked how these devices worked in the game at the time. However, as time in our reality progressed, the idea of minicomps began to become overshadowed by real world technology. I know that SI in the game is still science fiction, but even now we seem to be approaching that technological state pretty quickly. About the only aspect of minicomps that still seems futuristic are the agents. These \u201cprograms\u201d were a side character in games, with personalities and traits very similar to an actual person, though ChatGPT and Bard are approaching what I would consider an Agent. Still though, since Trinity takes place over 100 years in a version of our future, I would expect computer technology to have advanced more than it had in the original Trinity universe, even with the setbacks of the Aberrant War.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Century Gothic\">Jump to the latest version of Trinity, and you have some upgrades to minicomps. Augmented reality has been introduced, and the writers integrated wireless technology which was not ubiquitous like it is now when the original version of the game was written. These changes do make minicomps seem a little more futuristic, but I think that AR developments in our current reality are already starting to surpass what the authors of the latest version of Trinity had envisioned.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Century Gothic\">I am wondering what is next? What are some advancements to personal computing technology that we might see and can use for a setting that takes place 100 years in the future. Mind you, I\u2019m not looking for quantum computers that are inhabited by AI that can solve the mysteries of the universe. I am just wondering if technology like neural links should be common or not? Can nanotechnology make some personal computing functions seem like magic to someone from the 21<sup>st</sup> century? Is the personal computer still a small \u201cbrick\u201d? Can it be charged wirelessly?</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Century Gothic\">My biggest pet peeve though is the name. I have never liked the term minicomp, but I am struggling to come up with a new term that I like better to call these wonderful devices. I\u2019m hoping that if I can define them better by giving them some more advanced properties, maybe a name I do like better will come from the exercise.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Century Gothic\">Anyone have any ideas for more functions or names?</span><br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There is no good or evil. There is only instinct corrupted by intelligence.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5273-kingofdreams","name":"KingOfDreams","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5273_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T21:55:09-07:00","id":1515719,"title":"","content":"<i>'I know that SI in the game is still science fiction, but even now we seem to be approaching that technological state pretty quickly.'</i><br /> <br /> <i><b>Wrong</b></i>. By Secrets chapter in <b>Assassins</b> and <b>Anima</b>, Trinity universe had At LEAST two instances of True AI - in 2020s and 2080s. (Some can even argue in 1980s.) The only thing weird in <b>Aeon</b> era is Ban on true AI reaserch - technology is there, only humanity decide they will not risk once again this thing.<br /> <br /> To quote only from <b>Anima</b> - and remember that <b>Anima</b> is 2080s - <a href=\"https://theonyxpath.com/trinity-continuum-anima-terra-surge/\" target=\"_blank\"><b><i>Terra Surge</i></b> preview posted today</a>:<br /> <i>'Terra Surge has roots in traditional fantasy gaming, it offers so much more: a set of narrative AIs, called Narrators, that ensure each person experiences exactly what they want or need, with fully customizable strongholds, and a completely immersive \u2014 and expansive \u2014 virtual world full of fantastic creatures and landscapes.'</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-21-2023, 02:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-24T21:30:27-07:00","id":1516060,"title":"","content":"<i><b>'Wrong</b></i>.\u200b'<br /> <br /> I mis-wrote when I was talking about SI. What I meant to say was that in our reality, SI doesn't really exist yet, though it seems to be approaching quickly. I know that in the world of Trinity AI existed, and SI is prevalent. I like having AI as the potential boogeyman, and I don't mind the setting having that technology banned, or under very close scrutiny in the least.<br /> <br /> Wyrdhamster, I am curious if you have any ideas to change what Trinity society calls minicomps?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There is no good or evil. There is only instinct corrupted by intelligence.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5273-kingofdreams","name":"KingOfDreams","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5273_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T04:13:47-07:00","id":1516088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingOfDreams</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1515710-minicomp-moniker?p=1516060#post1516060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wyrdhamster, I am curious if you have any ideas to change what Trinity society calls minicomps?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would simply make Minicomp real AI Personal Agents. I'm not so afraid of General AI as game devs are.<br /> <br /> To explore idea more - look into <i><b>Mission Statements</b></i> book and OBC Metacorp subchapter - there is AI story hook there about long dead actor replica... \ud83d\ude0e","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T04:40:55-07:00","id":1516198,"title":"","content":"I personally thought that the minicomps could use a bit more leaning into the bio element of biotech. Many species of jellyfish are colony organisms that might be used as a basis for bringing together component functions for a unit. Then, have that device adhere to the user on the forearm or just behind the shoulder, with prehensile cables for secure access and wireless transmissions for trusted devices. Display by holo projection or contact lens interface could be the norm.<br /> <br /> Neural interface seems to leave a bad taste in humanity\u2019s mouth because of the events being outlined in Anima, but maybe we could work our way around that softly with neural induction contacts, or a symbiotic biotech organism that works on telepathic principles to convey data and acting as a buffer between user and outside data\u2026 like a biotech firewall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27972,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27972-gm-janus","user":"GM Janus","date":". 06-26-2023, 06:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27972-gm-janus","name":"GM Janus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}